Privacy Policy

Last updated: May 12, 2026

Pollito Productions operates the mobile application Backrooms - Breakout. This page informs users about our policies regarding the collection, use, and disclosure of information when using the Service.

1. Information Collection and Use

Backrooms - Breakout does not require account creation and does not directly collect personally identifiable information such as real names, addresses, phone numbers, or email addresses from players.

The game may store anonymous gameplay-related information, including:

leaderboard scores
survival times
optional player-chosen display names

Display names are filtered for inappropriate content before submission.

Participation in online leaderboards is completely optional.

2. Third-Party Service Providers

The app uses third-party services that may collect anonymous technical or device-related information in accordance with their own privacy policies.

These services may include:

Google Play Services
 — used for app distribution and platform services.
Google AdMob
 — used to serve advertisements, including rewarded ads.
Firebase Realtime Database
 — used for optional online leaderboard functionality.

These third-party services may collect information such as:

device identifiers
advertising identifiers
app interaction data
diagnostic or performance information
3. Local Storage

The Service may use local device storage to save gameplay information such as:

game progress
settings
unlocked features
local statistics

This information is stored locally on the user’s device.

4. Children’s Privacy

These Services are not directed toward children under the age of 13.

We do not knowingly collect personally identifiable information from children under 13. If we become aware that such information has been provided, we will take reasonable steps to delete it.

5. Security

We value user privacy and strive to use commercially acceptable means of protecting information. However, no method of electronic storage or internet transmission is completely secure, and we cannot guarantee absolute security.

6. Changes to This Privacy Policy

This Privacy Policy may be updated from time to time. Any changes will be posted on this page with an updated revision date.

